<h3>Electricians: Specificity Beats Generality</h3>

<p>Most electricians use "Electrician" as their primary category, and for good reason — it is the closest match to how most customers actually search. Variants like "Electrical Contractor" or "Electrical Installation Service" exist and can be the right choice in narrower cases, but "Electrician" is the safer default for a general residential electrical business.</p>

<p>More specific categories like "Electrical Installation Service" can outperform "Electrician" for narrowly matching searches (like "electrical installation"), but tend to underperform it for broad "electrician near me" searches, since they signal a narrower specialty than the generic term.</p>

<p><strong>Primary category recommendation:</strong> Use "Electrician" unless you exclusively perform a specialty. If you are solar-only, "Solar Energy Company" is the more accurate choice. If the large majority of your work is general residential electrical, "Electrician" wins.</p>

<p><strong>Secondary category stack worth considering:</strong></p>

<ol>
<li><strong>Electrical Installation Service</strong> - captures new construction and renovation searches</li>
<li><strong>Lighting Contractor</strong> - strong for outdoor lighting and commercial projects</li>
<li><strong>EV Charging Station Installer</strong> - a fast-growing category in electrical work</li>
<li><strong>Generator Shop</strong> - relevant if you install backup generators</li>
<li><strong>Security System Installer</strong> - only if you do low-voltage security work</li>
<li><strong>Home Automation Service</strong> - a growing category for smart home work</li>
</ol>

<p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> "EV Charging Station Installer" is still underused by many electrical contractors relative to how fast EV-charger-installation search demand has grown. If you do this work, adding the category early is a low-cost way to get ahead of competitors who have not caught on yet.</p>

<h3>Roofing Contractors: The Repair vs. Replacement Divide</h3>

<p>Roofing shows a clear split between repair-focused and replacement-focused businesses, and your primary category should reflect whichever one actually drives your revenue. "Roofing Contractor" is the safer general-purpose choice and tends to perform well for broad "roofing company near me" type searches.</p>

<p>"Roof Repair" as a primary category can sharpen relevance for repair- and leak-specific searches, but may underperform for "new roof" or replacement-intent searches. Specialty categories like "Metal Roofing Contractor" can dominate their narrow niche while becoming nearly invisible for generic roofing searches — only use them if that specialty is genuinely most of your business.</p>

