<h2>Recommendations: Your 30-Day GBP Category Optimization Plan</h2>

<p>Good advice without action is just trivia. Here is a concrete 30-day plan home service contractors can follow to optimize their GBP categories and attributes.</p>

<h3>Week 1: Audit and Baseline</h3>

<p><strong>Day 1-2: Document your current setup.</strong> Record your primary category, all secondary categories, attribute completion percentage, and current Map Pack position for your top 5 keywords. Use a tool like Local Falcon or BrightLocal to get accurate position data.</p>

<p><strong>Day 3-4: Study your top 3 competitors.</strong> Use the GMB Everywhere browser extension to see their exact categories. Document their primary, secondary, and any attributes they have enabled that you do not.</p>

<p><strong>Day 5-7: Identify category gaps.</strong> Compare your categories against the trade-specific recommendations in this guide. Ask: Is my primary category the most specific accurate option? Am I missing secondary categories that my competitors have? Are there newer categories Google has added that I should consider?</p>

<h3>Week 2: Implement Category Changes</h3>

<p><strong>Day 8: Change your primary category if needed.</strong> Only do this if you are moving to a more specific, more accurate option. Remember: primary category changes can cause a couple of weeks of volatility. Do not change during your busiest season.</p>

<p><strong>Day 9-10: Add or remove secondary categories.</strong> Aim for roughly 4-6 highly relevant secondary categories. Remove anything only loosely related to your business. Add any high-impact categories you are missing.</p>

<p><strong>Day 11-12: Update predefined services.</strong> Go through the Services section and select every predefined service that applies. Add custom services for anything not covered.</p>

<p><strong>Day 13-14: Enable all relevant attributes.</strong> Go through every attribute category in your GBP dashboard. Enable anything that is true and relevant, paying special attention to Service Options and Offerings.</p>

<h3>Week 3: Content and Review Alignment</h3>

<p><strong>Day 15-17: Align your website.</strong> Make sure your website's service pages mention the exact categories and services in your GBP. Google cross-references these signals.</p>

<p><strong>Day 18-19: Request category-specific reviews.</strong> When asking customers for reviews, mention the specific service they received. A review that says "Great drain cleaning service" reinforces your "Drain Cleaning Service" secondary category.</p>

<p><strong>Day 20-21: Post about your categories.</strong> Create Google Posts highlighting each of your core services. This reinforces category relevance through content signals.</p>

<h3>Week 4: Monitor and Adjust</h3>

<p><strong>Day 22-25: Track position changes.</strong> Check your Map Pack position regularly for your top 5 keywords. Expect some volatility for the first 10-14 days after category changes.</p>

<p><strong>Day 26-28: Measure traffic and engagement.</strong> Check your GBP insights for changes in profile views, direction requests, and phone calls. Compare against your Week 1 baseline.</p>

<p><strong>Day 29-30: Document and plan.</strong> Record what changed, what worked, and what did not. Set a calendar reminder to re-audit your categories in 90 days. Google adds new categories regularly, and your business evolves.</p>

